# Settings for scripts/dev-up, dev-down and dev-status (guide/06-local-dev.md).
#
# Copy this file to scripts/dev.env, which git ignores, and take the "# " off
# the lines you need. Every line is optional: with no file at all, dev-up
# builds leaf and starts it on 127.0.0.1:3777 with ./data and no tunnel.
#
# The file is read as plain NAME=value lines; it is not run as a shell script.
# Quotes around a value are allowed, "~/" at the start of a path is your home
# directory, a relative path starts at the repository root, and nothing else
# is expanded. A variable already set in your shell wins over its line here,
# so `LEAF_DEV_PORT=3999 scripts/dev-up` works for one run. A name that is
# not in this file is reported and ignored.
#
# To keep a second environment beside this one, write its settings in another
# file (with its own LEAF_DEV_PORT, LEAF_DEV_DATA_DIR and LEAF_DEV_RUN_DIR) and
# name that file in the shell: `LEAF_DEV_ENV_FILE=path scripts/dev-up`.
#
# No credential belongs here. leaf keeps the bot token, the client secret and
# the storage keys in leaf.conf in its data directory, written by the setup
# page, and these scripts never open that file.

# ---- leaf

# The port leaf listens on, on 127.0.0.1 only. `scripts/dev-up --port N`
# overrides it for one run. The tunnel's config has to send to the same port.
# LEAF_DEV_PORT=3777

# leaf's data directory (its DATA_DIR): where leaf.conf and leaf.db are kept.
# LEAF_DEV_DATA_DIR=data

# leaf's log level (its LOG_LEVEL): error, warn, info, debug or trace. Leave
# it at info for a first run: the setup code is logged at that level.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Register the bot's commands in this one server instead of globally (its
# DEV_GUILD_ID; guide/01-install.md, "Command registration"). The bot must be
# a member of that server.
# DEV_GUILD_ID=123456789012345678

# ---- the tunnel
#
# Set the first three together. Without LEAF_DEV_TUNNEL_CONFIG, dev-up starts
# no tunnel and leaf is reachable on this machine only.

# The cloudflared config of your named tunnel. dev-up runs
# `cloudflared tunnel --config <this file> run <name>`.
# LEAF_DEV_TUNNEL_CONFIG=~/.cloudflared/leaf-local.yml

# The tunnel's name. Leave it out to use the `tunnel:` line of the config.
# LEAF_DEV_TUNNEL_NAME=leaf-local

# The address the tunnel serves, the same one entered as the Public URL on
# leaf's setup page. dev-up waits until it answers.
# LEAF_DEV_PUBLIC_URL=https://leaf-local.example.com

# The cloudflared to run, when it is not the one on PATH.
# LEAF_DEV_CLOUDFLARED=cloudflared

# ---- the Android emulator (scripts/dev-up --emulator)

# The virtual device to boot (`emulator -list-avds` lists them).
# LEAF_DEV_AVD=leaf-pixel

# The Android SDK: the directory that holds emulator/ and platform-tools/.
# Homebrew's command-line tools are in the path below; Android Studio's SDK
# is ~/Library/Android/sdk on macOS and ~/Android/Sdk on Linux.
# ANDROID_HOME=/opt/homebrew/share/android-commandlinetools

# More arguments for the emulator, separated by spaces.
# LEAF_DEV_EMULATOR_ARGS=-no-snapshot-load -no-boot-anim

# ---- the scripts themselves

# Where dev-up keeps its pid files and logs. It is never the data directory.
# A second environment (another port, another data directory) needs its own.
# LEAF_DEV_RUN_DIR=.dev-run

# How long dev-up waits, in seconds, for leaf to answer, for the bot to leave
# "starting", for the public URL to answer through the tunnel and for Android
# to finish booting.
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_LEAF=30
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_GATEWAY=20
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_TUNNEL=60
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_EMULATOR=300

# How long dev-down waits, in seconds, after asking a process to stop before
# it kills it. The emulator has a wait of its own, because it saves its
# snapshot on the way out and a kill in the middle of that can spoil it.
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_STOP=15
# LEAF_DEV_WAIT_STOP_EMULATOR=120
